invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_limb.h
catches: p256_equiv_test_builtin
reason: the form of the add with carry that clang compiles keeps the carry
  of a + b and drops the carry of adding the carry in, so a limb sum of
  2^64 - 1 with a carry in of 1 returns 0 and no carry out. Nothing
  faults, and the field and the scalar go on computing with a value that
  is short by 2^64 at that limb. gcc for x86-64, which CI compiles with,
  reads another form, so bin/p256_equiv_test never compiles the line
  there: bin/p256_equiv_test_builtin names the form and holds every sum
  on it to p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    *carry = first | second;
--- new
    (void)second;
    *carry = first;
